<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/conflicts/16th-century">Conflicts &amp; Resolutions</a> · Battle</p><h1 class="enc-title">Battle of Solway Moss</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1542</span> · <a href="/centuries/16th-century">16th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Battle of Solway Moss was fought on 24 November 1542 near the River Esk on the English border, where a small English force routed a larger Scottish army sent by James V. Many Scottish nobles were captured. James V died a few weeks later, leaving his week-old daughter Mary as queen, and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/henry-viii-of-england">Henry VIII</a> then pressed for her marriage to his son Edward.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/battle-of-solway-moss.jpg" alt="Battle of Solway Moss" width="320" height="240" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Andrew Smith · CC BY-SA 2.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:The_River_Esk,_Arthuret_-_geograph.org.uk_-_1325304.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
